{"name":"Chocolate Truffle","hex":"#612e32","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate truffle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A confection having a center of ganache and an outer coating of powdered cocoa or chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate_truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A chocolate truffle is a French chocolate confectionery traditionally made with a chocolate ganache center and coated in cocoa powder, coconut, or chopped nuts. A chocolate truffle is handrolled into a spherical or ball shape. The name derives from the chocolate truffle's similarity in appearance to truffles, a tuber fungus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Truffles_with_nuts_and_chocolate_dusting_in_detail.jpg/330px-Truffles_with_nuts_and_chocolate_dusting_in_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_truffle","wikidata":"Q1063560"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"},{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle","wikidata":"Q2690965"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)","wikidata":"Q3309916"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg/500px-Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg/1280px-Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg/500px-Chocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate truffles with peanut butter filling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_truffles_with_peanut_butter_002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Maya glyph for cacao","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/